---
source: tests/cli.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stdout)"
---
Show a desktop notification to the user.

Prints {"sent":bool,"method":…,"reason":…}. Uses Herdr inside Herdr, else notify-send, else osascript; none available is not an error. Ignores --harness and --session.

Example: multiplexer-driver notify --message "build done"

Usage: multiplexer-driver notify [OPTIONS] --message <MESSAGE>

Options:
      --harness <HARNESS>
          Harness to drive. Required for workspace, pane, and raw

          Possible values:
          - tmux:  tmux
          - herdr: Herdr
          
          [env: MULTIPLEXER_DRIVER_HARNESS=]

      --message <MESSAGE>
          Notification body

      --session <SESSION>
          Harness server to use: a Herdr session name or a tmux -L socket name. Unset uses the ambient server
          
          [env: MULTIPLEXER_DRIVER_SESSION=]

      --title <TITLE>
          Notification title
          
          [default: Overseer]

      --pretty
          Indent single-object output. Lists stay JSON Lines

      --sound <SOUND>
          Sound: none, done, or request (Herdr only)
          
          [possible values: none, done, request]

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Diagnostics level on stderr: debug, info, warn, or error
          
          [env: RUST_LOG=]
          [default: warn]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
